WEBVTT

01:03.229 --> 01:05.982
GENIE, MAKE A WISH

01:24.292 --> 01:26.461
PLEASE RETURN YOUR ID
AND YOUR LOCKER AND BUILDING KEYS

01:26.544 --> 01:29.297
Gu Bo-gyeong, your actions
are unacceptable. You are fired, got it?

01:29.380 --> 01:31.800
Thanks to you, the branch's
highest earning client is gone!

01:34.969 --> 01:38.098
Fuck!

01:39.516 --> 01:40.391
A genie?

01:41.434 --> 01:44.604
What are you talking about? Our channel
went viral because of the skeleton.

01:44.687 --> 01:48.066
Exactly! And the genie made it so
I'd uncover the skeleton.

01:48.149 --> 01:50.693
I'm being serious.
How else could I find that body?

01:51.194 --> 01:53.238
Out of the blue like that? Huh?

01:53.738 --> 01:55.698
You have to believe me!

01:55.782 --> 01:58.868
We only have
two more chances left, Da-jin.

01:58.952 --> 02:00.745
We both have top degrees.

02:00.829 --> 02:03.039
We gotta think long and hard,

02:03.123 --> 02:05.458
come up with a way
to turn our lives around. Right?

02:13.716 --> 02:15.426
Seeing as it's a wish,

02:15.510 --> 02:17.303
what about getting
on a billionaire's will?

02:17.387 --> 02:21.474
You gotta think bigger.
We should be the billionaires.

02:22.392 --> 02:25.520
Wait a minute. Just how rich
is the richest person in Korea?

02:25.603 --> 02:28.523
We don't need that much money, do we?
We're not business people.

02:28.606 --> 02:30.108
Say, we have two kids.

02:30.191 --> 02:33.069
Private schools, homes for them,
setting them up when they get married?

02:33.153 --> 02:35.280
That's tons of money.
And what about when we're old?

02:35.363 --> 02:37.782
Yeah, you're right. Better to be prepared.

02:38.449 --> 02:41.202
You're sure there's no stipulations
or conditions?

02:41.286 --> 02:44.164
Isn't there usually some catch
like "careful what you wish for,"

02:44.247 --> 02:47.458
when it comes to fables involving genies?
"It's gonna bite you in the ass."

02:48.835 --> 02:51.462
What if there's something like that?

02:52.255 --> 02:54.299
-It'd be helpful if we could ask.
-Hey!

02:54.966 --> 02:57.177
What happens if he says
that counts as one of my wishes?

02:58.720 --> 03:00.013
-You're right.
-Mm!

03:02.765 --> 03:06.978
Then, why don't we each think of a wish,
so you get one and I can get one?

03:07.061 --> 03:07.896
What?

03:08.897 --> 03:11.900
-But why would we do that?
-Um…

03:11.983 --> 03:14.611
I wouldn't have told you
if you were gonna ask that.

03:16.196 --> 03:17.947
But we're married, so isn't it a given?

03:18.531 --> 03:20.825
We can make money,
but some things, money can't fix.

03:21.910 --> 03:23.536
What can't money fix for us?

03:25.038 --> 03:26.206
Like my dad's cancer.

03:26.706 --> 03:30.543
Come on!
Doctors can do anything these days!

03:30.627 --> 03:33.338
Why would you waste a wish on that, huh?

03:33.421 --> 03:34.797
Anyway, money can fix that.

03:35.506 --> 03:37.133
Yeah, but it's terminal.

03:37.842 --> 03:39.344
Terminal means no hope for recovery.

03:39.427 --> 03:42.138
It's not like he's on hospice
right this second or anything.

03:42.722 --> 03:43.890
And besides, our views.

03:43.973 --> 03:46.100
We're gonna be so rich soon.

03:46.184 --> 03:47.727
Let's just wait a few months.

03:47.810 --> 03:49.771
Hold off on making wishes, okay?

03:49.854 --> 03:51.105
No, it's not okay.

03:52.065 --> 03:53.107
It's not okay!

04:26.808 --> 04:27.684
Khalid!

04:28.309 --> 04:29.394
Khalid!

04:30.895 --> 04:33.022
I saw the shaytan. I saw it all!

04:33.690 --> 04:34.941
He was killing everyone.

04:35.692 --> 04:38.528
It was the most beautiful thing
I've ever seen, Father.

04:38.611 --> 04:41.572
Tell me what happened to that girl.
Did you hurt her?

04:42.156 --> 04:43.324
I have no pain anymore.

04:43.908 --> 04:46.286
It's even easy to breathe
in this new body.

04:47.453 --> 04:49.664
But I do not have a power like Iblis.

04:49.747 --> 04:51.416
I no longer have my abilities.

04:52.000 --> 04:55.461
What am I to even do
with a powerless eternal body?

05:10.143 --> 05:12.478
The end is near!

05:13.354 --> 05:15.023
Foolish sinners!

05:15.815 --> 05:18.818
Judgment Day is upon us!

05:19.360 --> 05:22.155
The angels are warning us!

05:22.238 --> 05:25.283
-You get a pass today.
-Heed my word, all of you.

05:25.366 --> 05:27.577
I have got more important matters.

05:27.660 --> 05:30.246
Only then shall your soul be sa--

05:44.844 --> 05:47.472
You said I stole your feather
before my imprisonment.

05:48.139 --> 05:50.516
Are you going on again
about that damn feather?

05:50.600 --> 05:53.644
-I keep telling you I don't know--
-I now know what I used it for.

05:54.228 --> 05:56.105
The inside of my lamp
is covered in writing.

05:56.189 --> 05:58.733
The floors, the walls, everywhere.
It's a lot.

06:01.110 --> 06:03.738
You figured that out?

06:03.821 --> 06:05.907
Yes. But when could I have done that?

06:07.241 --> 06:08.242
I don't remember it.

06:10.036 --> 06:15.541
So… make sure we are punished right,

06:15.625 --> 06:17.043
you and me.

06:17.126 --> 06:19.212
That wish Ki Ka-young made so long ago

06:20.213 --> 06:22.423
was fulfilled. Am I right?

06:24.133 --> 06:27.011
He brought her back to life
so he could complete her last wish.

06:27.595 --> 06:31.849
And then I see her again,
after she's been reincarnated. That right?

06:33.559 --> 06:36.104
If my rage was enough
to obliterate a whole city…

06:38.523 --> 06:42.151
HABIBTI

06:42.235 --> 06:43.820
…the one I loved had died.

06:44.612 --> 06:45.613
Ka-young did.

06:47.990 --> 06:49.450
I was in love with Ka-young.

06:49.534 --> 06:51.744
-Isn't that right?
-So what?

06:52.787 --> 06:55.998
-We playing games now? Why should I care?
-What of her lifespan?

06:57.458 --> 06:59.127
-You gone crazy?
-How much time is left?

06:59.669 --> 07:00.670
I beg you.

07:02.380 --> 07:05.758
-Help me so I can be ready.
-All because of a lump of clay!

07:06.801 --> 07:08.886
Did you learn nothing
from Shadi's pitiful fate?

07:08.970 --> 07:10.263
I learned so much.

07:12.056 --> 07:15.351
I've learned to do everything in my power
to not kill Khalid the second I see him.

07:16.477 --> 07:18.980
Shadi is willing to sacrifice himself
for his son.

07:20.440 --> 07:21.732
His love is so strong.

07:23.359 --> 07:24.777
It stabs right to his core.

07:28.364 --> 07:29.740
So proud and haughty.

07:30.658 --> 07:31.659
If you're that impatient,

07:31.742 --> 07:34.412
then pluck my eyes out
to see the truth for yourself. I dare you.

07:34.495 --> 07:37.665
I wonder what possible reason
he could've had for forgiving you.

07:47.258 --> 07:49.969
You'll be subjected to judgment soon!

07:50.720 --> 07:52.930
Who will achieve salvation?

08:14.202 --> 08:16.204
I was gathering intel
about the immortal one.

08:17.371 --> 08:20.583
I felt that your intentions
maybe were aligned with his.

08:21.459 --> 08:24.462
He is trying to climb his way
up the ranks at any cost.

08:25.087 --> 08:28.466
Iblis and Ki Ka-young grow even closer
to the truth of their shared history.

08:29.759 --> 08:34.222
What can I do when even my beast
is off the radar? Huh, Irem?

08:34.305 --> 08:38.351
Then, if you could narrow
your plans down some more--

08:38.434 --> 08:39.977
I'm doing that now.

08:42.313 --> 08:45.691
Listen carefully…
Oh, wait, you still can't.

08:48.152 --> 08:49.737
Read my lips, then.

08:51.239 --> 08:55.535
The immortal one will use his father
to plunge the world into sleep once again.

08:56.661 --> 08:58.955
There's something you'll have to do
when that day comes.

08:59.580 --> 09:01.082
That's all I expect you to do.

09:02.667 --> 09:03.668
Got it?

09:06.754 --> 09:08.839
Yes. Understood.

09:14.262 --> 09:15.596
Hmm.

09:16.347 --> 09:17.473
These kids.

09:19.225 --> 09:20.685
ELDEST

09:22.436 --> 09:23.604
Hello.

09:23.688 --> 09:26.899
I brought you a few homemade dishes,
but the code isn't working.

09:26.983 --> 09:29.402
You forgot to tell me that you updated it.

09:29.485 --> 09:33.239
What? I told you not to come.
I told you my wife is away on a cruise.

09:33.322 --> 09:35.074
That's why I brought all this food to you.

09:35.658 --> 09:37.743
-It needs to be refri--
-Just leave it at the door.

09:37.827 --> 09:40.413
My wife doesn't like strangers
going in and out of our home.

09:40.496 --> 09:42.999
You can't speak to me like that!
I'm a stranger?

09:43.082 --> 09:44.917
You see me that way, huh?

09:45.001 --> 09:46.210
You little…

09:48.588 --> 09:50.172
Oh, my. Stop eating and start peeling.

09:53.926 --> 09:56.220
Why aren't you going
to visit your son, the judge?

09:56.846 --> 09:59.265
Yeah. He was going on and on about

09:59.348 --> 10:01.559
staying over and joining them
on some cruise.

10:01.642 --> 10:04.645
I don't have the energy. I just came back.

10:04.729 --> 10:07.523
Oh, my, how lovely. How lucky you are.

10:09.692 --> 10:11.319
Huh? What's this?

10:13.863 --> 10:14.739
OH PAN-GEUM

10:14.822 --> 10:17.992
I think I'll be traveling
even farther than Hawaii.

10:18.868 --> 10:21.579
-Please take good care of my Ka-young.
-Where is she off to now?

10:21.662 --> 10:23.748
Her daughter must be
treating her very well.

10:25.041 --> 10:27.293
Well, if it's not even Hawaii,
how nice could it be?

10:27.877 --> 10:31.130
Sounds like such a hassle to travel
at our age. What's so great about that?

10:31.714 --> 10:35.384
Hawaii? That tiny island?
I could go tomorrow if I wanted to.

10:35.468 --> 10:37.011
My eldest son is a judge,

10:37.094 --> 10:39.555
and my younger son
is an executive at a top firm,

10:39.639 --> 10:42.808
and their children are all geniuses.

10:42.892 --> 10:44.060
Ok-nam is a mess.

10:44.602 --> 10:47.563
Dropped her whole life,
ran away 'cause of her child.

10:49.065 --> 10:51.776
If anyone thinks
they could've done better than I did,

10:51.859 --> 10:53.444
then just come forward and prove it.

10:53.527 --> 10:56.614
Yes, of course. I'm with you.

10:56.697 --> 10:59.367
We all know. We all agree with you.

11:01.118 --> 11:02.453
AN BOK-JA

11:04.038 --> 11:08.459
Don't worry about Ka-young.
Send us some photos of your new place.

11:09.210 --> 11:12.046
Where's my daughter gone to?

11:13.964 --> 11:16.175
She changed her number without telling me.

11:19.553 --> 11:22.431
-What's that smell? Baeksuk?
-Yes.

11:23.265 --> 11:25.226
Tell that lanky fellow that it's ready.

11:28.688 --> 11:32.274
I hope you will continue to get along
with my dear Ka-young.

11:32.358 --> 11:35.736
Please watch over her, don't pick fights.

11:35.820 --> 11:39.407
If she behaves in a rude manner,
try to respond with kindness.

11:43.828 --> 11:44.787
I get the legs.

11:44.870 --> 11:47.623
Oh, come on now.

11:47.707 --> 11:50.209
Just share them.
We're all friends here. Mm.

11:50.793 --> 11:52.503
We should be sharing everything.

11:53.170 --> 11:57.383
Whether you're happy or sad,
for better or for worse, no matter what.

11:57.466 --> 11:59.677
What's this rule?
I always get the chicken legs.

11:59.760 --> 12:01.887
Goodness' sake! Just let him eat it!

12:01.971 --> 12:03.973
You know it's important to share!

12:04.056 --> 12:05.808
So what? The legs are always mine!

12:06.726 --> 12:09.061
Don't you dare touch those.

12:12.481 --> 12:13.315
Spit it out.

12:17.486 --> 12:19.363
Still want it?

12:19.447 --> 12:21.031
-I said, spit.
-No.

12:21.699 --> 12:24.034
Want me to kill you?

12:25.786 --> 12:27.747
-I want you to not kill me.
-Give me the chicken!

12:28.330 --> 12:30.958
-Don't be a child!
-Give me the chicken now!

12:31.041 --> 12:33.544
-I said, don't be a child.
-Stop repeating things!

12:33.627 --> 12:36.547
There's so much chemistry.
That's all you need.

12:36.630 --> 12:38.174
Get over here!

12:52.855 --> 12:55.858
Mm. This word here comes up the most.

12:55.941 --> 12:58.319
Is this habibti? "My true love"?

12:58.402 --> 12:59.236
Huh?

13:00.029 --> 13:01.155
Uh-huh.

13:01.822 --> 13:03.616
You don't remember,
yet you're sure it's me?

13:03.699 --> 13:05.451
-Mm?
-You know it's equally likely

13:05.534 --> 13:07.495
that it's about Jinniya. 50/50.

13:09.038 --> 13:12.458
We've already kissed.
Shouldn't you have asked this earlier?

13:14.460 --> 13:15.419
If it's about Jinniya,

13:17.379 --> 13:19.256
you will die for wasting my valuable time.

13:21.091 --> 13:22.510
So hurry up with finding the truth.

13:24.178 --> 13:27.223
Look at this one.
You spent every night sewing

13:27.807 --> 13:31.393
so you'll have new garments for
your return to Goryeo.

13:32.520 --> 13:33.354
Sewing?

13:33.938 --> 13:36.649
Hmm. I guess I must have liked needles
back then too.

13:37.775 --> 13:39.360
Mm?

13:40.027 --> 13:41.195
Where is Khalid's name?

13:41.862 --> 13:43.906
Here and here.

13:44.907 --> 13:45.741
Why?

13:45.825 --> 13:48.994
Because, in Korea, it's bad luck
for names to be written in red.

13:50.162 --> 13:52.957
Little shit.
If he started his mission this long ago,

13:54.250 --> 13:56.043
we're far less equipped than we thought.

13:59.171 --> 14:00.965
There is something that we do have.

14:01.048 --> 14:03.008
No matter how much info Khalid has on us,

14:03.092 --> 14:05.261
ultimately, you're making the wish,
not him.

14:07.721 --> 14:08.848
Let's get out of here.

14:09.932 --> 14:11.851
From now on, make sure
you always have the lamp.

14:13.894 --> 14:16.564
So, what, I should carry it around?

14:16.647 --> 14:18.315
I guess it could be a container

14:18.983 --> 14:20.192
to hold curry.

14:20.734 --> 14:22.152
That's believable, right?

14:22.236 --> 14:23.946
That's why…

14:25.489 --> 14:26.323
There.

14:27.741 --> 14:30.160
Well, I've seen bottles like this
carried around.

14:31.328 --> 14:33.622
-The adaptable type.
-Mm-hmm.

14:37.126 --> 14:39.461
I guess time is running out.
He'll strike soon.

14:44.133 --> 14:47.595
On that matter,
I need you to listen carefully.

14:47.678 --> 14:51.056
Khalid will definitely try to bind me
again, and he will use Shadi.

14:52.057 --> 14:55.436
So if he does tie me up,
and I can't help you,

14:57.313 --> 14:59.773
you must spend your final wish
on saving yourself.

15:00.983 --> 15:04.028
The wish must be righteous. All right?

15:07.072 --> 15:09.575
So you've already decided
what your plan is.

15:13.787 --> 15:15.289
But I refuse to let you go.

15:17.958 --> 15:20.044
Too bad, I thought that would work.

15:27.760 --> 15:29.511
I'm just so curious.

15:30.095 --> 15:32.765
Do psychopaths really not know
what love is?

15:32.848 --> 15:35.559
Like, being willing to sacrifice yourself
for another?

15:35.643 --> 15:36.852
I think I could kill…

15:37.895 --> 15:39.063
for another person.

15:40.481 --> 15:42.483
Does that count as love?

15:42.566 --> 15:44.985
Wow, hot damn! Hey, Da-jin, come look.

15:45.069 --> 15:47.780
Our interview with the psychopath
is viral. It's popping off.

15:48.697 --> 15:51.200
It's the ninth most trending video!

15:51.283 --> 15:54.244
They've even made it into a meme
in the comments.

15:54.954 --> 15:58.040
"I worked late for my manager.
Does that count as love?"

15:58.791 --> 16:01.627
"I binge ate for my boyfriend.
Does that count as love?"

16:02.211 --> 16:04.421
"I only ate the pie crust
and left the middle for--"

16:04.505 --> 16:06.507
Just the crust? That's mental.

16:06.590 --> 16:08.217
What the hell?

16:08.300 --> 16:10.010
Oh, that's hilarious.

16:10.094 --> 16:11.887
-So, what?
-Let's see…

16:12.554 --> 16:14.181
Have you decided about the wish?

16:15.516 --> 16:18.143
Are we still talking about that?

16:18.686 --> 16:19.979
Seriously, I'm over it.

16:20.521 --> 16:23.816
Let's enjoy our fame for a little while!

16:26.568 --> 16:27.444
I can't.

16:30.406 --> 16:31.824
I think we should get a divorce.

16:32.741 --> 16:34.535
-Huh?
-You've two wishes left, don't you?

16:35.369 --> 16:37.162
I would like one. It'll be alimony.

16:37.746 --> 16:38.664
A divorce?

16:39.415 --> 16:41.333
Come on, you've gone nuts.

16:42.209 --> 16:45.713
Huh? You can't possibly mean it.
They're my wishes, my choice.

16:46.296 --> 16:48.007
-It's nothing to do with you.
-Oh, yeah?

16:48.841 --> 16:50.342
And us being married is what?

16:51.510 --> 16:52.344
You asshole.

16:53.595 --> 16:55.889
What? Wait a minute, the fuck you say?

16:58.058 --> 17:00.811
So this person really is Ms. Oh Pan-geum?

17:00.894 --> 17:02.813
Yes! That's Oh Pan-geum.

17:02.896 --> 17:05.190
Third daughter of the family in Bukcheon.

17:05.274 --> 17:07.818
Ah, she was such a pretty young lady
in Hadong.

17:07.901 --> 17:09.737
She moved to Seoul when she got married.

17:09.820 --> 17:11.864
Oh, I know that smile.
That's her, all right.

17:11.947 --> 17:14.199
Her husband was from Chungcheong-do.

17:14.283 --> 17:17.161
Last I heard, their daughters
had families of their own.

17:18.078 --> 17:19.121
Let me see that.

17:20.748 --> 17:24.168
Oh, oh! This was
when she was a young lady.

17:24.752 --> 17:26.879
Why are you looking for her anyway?
Is she okay?

17:27.463 --> 17:29.381
-Did Pan-geum pass away?
-Hey.

17:30.507 --> 17:32.926
No. She's in great health.

17:33.010 --> 17:34.636
-Good to hear.
-Good.

17:40.309 --> 17:42.853
What does he do for a living?
I'm not quite sure yet.

17:42.936 --> 17:45.272
It's strange he's always asked me
what my wish is.

17:45.355 --> 17:47.107
Oh, my goodness,
my teeth got younger too!

17:47.691 --> 17:49.860
Just don't ask me anything
about the siblings.

17:49.943 --> 17:50.903
My deal?

17:50.986 --> 17:53.822
I can say one thing for sure.
He's not a real man.

17:54.448 --> 17:56.700
If I'm not to ask questions
about all this,

17:58.243 --> 18:02.331
and he's not human like we are,
and he gives us wishes to make…

18:08.712 --> 18:11.882
Wow. It's just so unreal, I'm speechless.

18:14.885 --> 18:18.764
Don't! Wear those out.
I just wanna buy you something, okay?

18:19.348 --> 18:22.351
You deserve them.
Wear these and go anywhere you want.

18:23.143 --> 18:24.436
Anywhere in the world.

18:25.771 --> 18:27.147
Just trust your instincts.

18:28.690 --> 18:29.566
Hmm?

18:36.448 --> 18:37.699
Mi-ju is…

18:40.744 --> 18:41.829
Pan-geum?

19:28.417 --> 19:31.670
Ka-young,
this jar here is the doenjang jar.

19:32.754 --> 19:34.673
Open the lid once a month.

19:34.756 --> 19:36.925
Check under the top layer of salt

19:37.009 --> 19:39.720
to make sure no mold
is growing on the surface

19:39.803 --> 19:41.638
or that no bugs have gotten in.

19:47.019 --> 19:50.439
When the weather is nice,
leave the lid open to let sunlight in.

19:50.981 --> 19:52.941
This jar here is the soy sauce jar.

19:53.984 --> 19:56.570
If you see white spots of mold developing,

19:56.653 --> 20:00.657
scoop them away before boiling
the soy sauce and pouring it back in.

20:25.724 --> 20:29.561
That means I'll last until next spring.

20:30.687 --> 20:31.897
I can make that work.

20:33.440 --> 20:36.485
Could be an accident, or an illness.

20:38.403 --> 20:40.906
There's nothing strange
about dying at this age.

20:44.034 --> 20:46.536
Oh, you're up. You need more sleep.

20:47.246 --> 20:48.872
You don't work today. Go back to sleep.

20:48.956 --> 20:50.874
I need to do some woodworking.

20:52.542 --> 20:55.587
Grandma, why do you keep looking
at that tree?

21:19.611 --> 21:20.654
Oh, hi!

21:20.737 --> 21:23.031
I don't know
if I should fix that hole or not.

21:23.615 --> 21:24.658
'Cause from here,

21:25.742 --> 21:27.369
if feels almost like

21:28.036 --> 21:28.954
I'm a corpse.

21:29.037 --> 21:31.373
Oh, you're such a romantic, aren't you?

21:37.379 --> 21:39.298
Would this mean we're buried together?

21:40.007 --> 21:41.883
That's how you'd react
to something like this?

21:48.598 --> 21:51.018
What do you say
we take to the skies again?

21:51.727 --> 21:52.602
You go ahead.

21:54.730 --> 21:57.399
I need to take Grandma
to visit Seoul tomorrow.

21:57.482 --> 21:58.775
You go for a ride,

22:00.152 --> 22:01.153
and fix the roof.

22:02.237 --> 22:03.238
Seoul? Why?

22:04.990 --> 22:08.327
Grandma deserves better memories of us,
ones that are normal and nice.

22:12.581 --> 22:13.415
All right.

22:19.713 --> 22:21.506
I should get some like that too.

22:27.596 --> 22:28.930
Oh. Oh, oh!

22:30.265 --> 22:31.600
K.O.

22:31.683 --> 22:33.685
Hell yeah! K.O. win!

22:37.689 --> 22:38.774
I gotta go home now.

22:39.358 --> 22:41.777
Wait a second, you can't leave.
I haven't won yet.

22:41.860 --> 22:45.113
You should go home soon too, Mister.
Home's so nice now.

22:46.698 --> 22:48.867
That's a pretty new mindset for you.

22:49.826 --> 22:52.162
-What, you bought a house?
-Hey, not funny.

22:53.872 --> 22:55.707
You have to promise not to tell.

22:56.875 --> 22:59.795
An angel granted a wish for me.

22:59.878 --> 23:02.506
Momma's boyfriend is gone now.

23:03.715 --> 23:07.386
That's why I'm cutting back on the arcade
and stuff, so Mom doesn't worry.

23:10.389 --> 23:12.641
Well, that's a side effect
I didn't consider.

23:14.810 --> 23:15.852
Kim Sang-hyeok.

23:18.105 --> 23:19.106
I've had a lot of fun.

23:20.065 --> 23:21.942
You've been a real brother, you know.

23:24.653 --> 23:25.529
Don't forget it.

23:26.405 --> 23:27.406
What are you saying?

23:27.989 --> 23:30.784
I said that I'd cut back,
not that I wasn't gonna play at all.

23:31.535 --> 23:32.619
See you tomorrow.

23:50.679 --> 23:52.389
You're not going?

23:53.014 --> 23:55.517
What's wrong? It's the department store.

23:56.143 --> 23:59.604
-Their new winter lines are out.
-I have enough clothes.

24:00.272 --> 24:01.940
Enough to last until February.

24:03.692 --> 24:04.860
Instead…

24:06.653 --> 24:07.988
I have an idea.

24:09.656 --> 24:10.657
Okay, let's hear it.

24:13.160 --> 24:14.369
This was your idea?

24:16.163 --> 24:17.330
Why?

24:17.414 --> 24:20.250
I want you to remember me as pretty.

24:21.751 --> 24:23.628
Gosh, I'm pretty. Am I not?

24:24.254 --> 24:25.255
Cute, right?

24:27.799 --> 24:28.967
"Remember me"?

24:30.969 --> 24:33.472
Why does it seem like
she and I have the same idea?

24:36.892 --> 24:38.185
Cheese.

24:38.268 --> 24:40.812
Eh.

24:41.813 --> 24:45.108
Do it, like this.
Hey, come on, come on. Eeh.

24:45.192 --> 24:47.068
Ah. Uh, how about this?

24:48.236 --> 24:49.905
Do this.

24:53.450 --> 24:54.784
I love them!

24:55.744 --> 24:56.745
Pretty.

24:58.788 --> 25:00.290
Why bother taking these?

25:00.373 --> 25:02.501
Why not? They're so much fun.

25:03.543 --> 25:05.921
Grab us some coffee.
Let's enjoy ourselves a little longer.

25:06.505 --> 25:09.216
Go and get us
two really sweet lattes, okay?

25:10.091 --> 25:11.218
-Okay, sure.
-Okay.

25:13.803 --> 25:16.139
Oh, wow.

26:10.318 --> 26:12.320
Your marquee needs new bulbs on one side.

26:12.946 --> 26:14.656
Are you trying to dissuade new clients?

26:16.408 --> 26:17.742
Yes, I saw that.

26:19.619 --> 26:20.912
I smell gamja-tang.

26:22.330 --> 26:23.415
Is it Wednesday?

26:23.498 --> 26:26.209
I got it to go. It's a different spot.

26:27.294 --> 26:28.128
I'm hungry.

26:30.130 --> 26:32.299
I thought you were angry with me.

26:33.049 --> 26:34.217
This is your routine.

26:41.266 --> 26:43.226
CHEONGPUNG VILLAGE HALL

26:48.148 --> 26:50.442
Oh Pan-geum? How is Hawaii?

26:51.776 --> 26:53.069
Yes, Ka-young is great.

26:53.695 --> 26:55.614
Have you tried the coconut shrimp yet?

26:56.323 --> 26:57.866
Oh, sounds good.

26:59.200 --> 27:02.412
Yeah, right. She didn't go someplace else.

27:02.495 --> 27:04.581
Still in Hawaii. That proves it.

27:07.000 --> 27:07.876
Oh?

27:39.366 --> 27:42.702
I think that I'm gonna stop holding
these rites.

27:44.079 --> 27:45.330
It's time for me to stop.

27:47.916 --> 27:51.169
-Why?
-Well, because, I'm just done.

27:52.504 --> 27:54.255
If I should die soon,

27:54.339 --> 27:57.509
don't bother with doing ancestral rites
for me. Don't give me anything.

27:58.760 --> 28:01.137
All I want is my ashes spread around.

28:03.807 --> 28:06.726
Just leave it, go on.
Flight's at 12:00, yes?

28:06.810 --> 28:08.144
Quarter to 12:00.

28:09.771 --> 28:12.148
The chief will keep an eye on you,
so stay by his side.

28:12.232 --> 28:14.025
I won't be gone long. All right?

28:14.609 --> 28:16.319
Okay. Go have fun.

28:23.743 --> 28:25.745
I can't remember what my wish was for.

28:26.663 --> 28:29.499
But I think it resulted in a bad ending.

28:30.083 --> 28:31.251
So I'm scared.

28:55.233 --> 28:56.359
Excuse me, ma'am.

28:56.443 --> 28:59.821
You've been rubbing this lamp
for three hours now.

29:00.363 --> 29:01.823
It's only right that you buy it.

29:02.490 --> 29:04.033
It's yours for 1,000 dirhams.

29:04.784 --> 29:06.703
I cannot speak Arabic.

29:07.412 --> 29:08.872
How about a discount?

29:11.833 --> 29:13.752
Daily report. Keeping a close watch.

29:13.835 --> 29:16.504
-Nothing to worry about here.
-Thank you.

29:21.885 --> 29:24.512
Hey! What do you want? What?

29:29.934 --> 29:32.687
TISAH

29:47.243 --> 29:48.077
Oh.

30:02.926 --> 30:04.344
CONSULATE EMERGENCY HOTLINE

30:24.405 --> 30:26.074
Could you leave my jar alone?

30:31.037 --> 30:33.581
-I knew you were avoiding me.
-What if I was?

30:33.665 --> 30:36.709
You're gonna keep calling me like a dog?
You've barely lived a century.

30:37.460 --> 30:41.589
You recognized me the minute you saw me.
You called me "that little shit."

30:42.340 --> 30:44.050
When exactly did we meet before?

30:45.093 --> 30:46.594
I need you to tell me everything.

30:47.178 --> 30:48.513
This is my first wish.

30:48.596 --> 30:51.224
Sweetie, what are you talking about?

30:52.141 --> 30:54.143
Not every genie grants wishes, you know.

30:54.853 --> 30:57.355
Only Iblis can give you wishes.

31:01.442 --> 31:02.902
Then I'll ask nicely.

31:07.240 --> 31:08.366
Why is your face doing that?

31:10.326 --> 31:13.955
Iblis has a way of making us feel
dejected. His mere presence does it.

31:14.831 --> 31:17.125
He stood right at the front lines
during the war.

31:21.254 --> 31:23.923
And, thanks to him,
we were saved from the angels.

31:24.632 --> 31:27.719
We all acquiesced and bowed to humanity.

31:27.802 --> 31:29.679
As you know, he refused
and was sent to hell.

31:30.430 --> 31:32.557
So it's hard to believe
one human's death could cause

31:32.640 --> 31:34.267
the destruction of a whole city.

31:34.893 --> 31:36.227
I couldn't understand it.

31:37.270 --> 31:39.689
He destroyed a city because of me?

31:42.525 --> 31:43.526
Yes, that's right.

31:44.152 --> 31:47.572
Golden rain swept a city away.
So, yes, you were that little shit.

31:49.449 --> 31:51.409
Gold rain poured?

31:51.492 --> 31:54.037
It was a truly dazzling,
beautiful hell on earth.

31:54.621 --> 31:56.080
"The wrath of Iblis" they called it.

31:56.664 --> 31:58.583
Why does his wrath come out as gold?

32:00.376 --> 32:01.210
I don't know.

32:02.462 --> 32:04.672
-Meaning what?
-I don't want to know.

32:06.841 --> 32:10.094
You don't find it strange that Iblis
has no memories of that time?

32:12.263 --> 32:15.058
-Ah. I'm sorry.
-Don't come back if you mean it.

32:15.683 --> 32:19.479
We're now even when I danced for joy
when Muttalib killed you. Get out.

32:20.229 --> 32:22.982
Ah. The guy who killed me back then.

32:26.277 --> 32:28.446
I appreciate it. Mm.

32:30.823 --> 32:33.534
Any chance Iblis called you habibti
when you were together?

32:37.622 --> 32:39.332
Any chance you've had bees pelt your face?

32:41.084 --> 32:43.836
So I'm the one.

32:52.011 --> 32:54.514
Irem! Irem!

33:00.770 --> 33:02.313
Whew.

33:04.691 --> 33:07.151
I was in bed when you called.
I just threw this on.

33:08.403 --> 33:10.863
-Have a seat.
-Okay.

33:14.450 --> 33:16.536
I can't be sure about it,

33:16.619 --> 33:19.622
but there are peculiar things going on
that they aren't telling us.

33:19.706 --> 33:22.208
There's something you'll have to do
when that day comes.

33:23.084 --> 33:26.629
Getting to business before cotton candy?
What could it possibly be?

33:28.047 --> 33:30.008
You and I serve our masters faithfully.

33:30.591 --> 33:33.011
So if a time comes
when you will have to act decisively,

33:33.094 --> 33:36.472
it is crucial that your decision
is worthy of your master's strength.

33:37.140 --> 33:39.017
I'll do the same as well. All right?

33:40.727 --> 33:43.354
I got all fancy for you.
Odd way to get dumped.

33:45.273 --> 33:47.859
You said you were in bed.
Your ears are showing.

33:47.942 --> 33:49.027
I like to sleep this way.

33:49.110 --> 33:50.903
-Check those out.
-Those are cute.

33:51.487 --> 33:53.573
-I want a pair.
-Let's get them.

33:57.660 --> 33:59.704
MY CHANNEL

33:59.787 --> 34:01.789
SKY FARM LIFE

34:10.089 --> 34:13.551
NEW PASSWORD: 1 GENIE WISH IS MINE!

34:18.097 --> 34:19.932
PASSWORD CHANGED

34:26.022 --> 34:27.940
YOUR CHANNEL HAS BEEN DELETED

34:30.401 --> 34:33.821
Hey, Choi Da-jin! Da-jin, Da-jin! Hey!
What's wrong with our channel?

34:33.905 --> 34:37.950
Quickly. You-- You gotta look.
The whole channel was erased like that!

34:38.034 --> 34:40.453
The fuck is going on? What the hell!

34:42.288 --> 34:45.458
You think we got reported?
Why were we reported?

34:45.541 --> 34:47.877
-This'll be the death of me!
-We weren't.

34:47.960 --> 34:49.337
I decided to delete my account.

34:51.172 --> 34:52.548
Have you lost your mind?

34:52.632 --> 34:55.051
Do you know what it took
to get all that traffic?

34:55.593 --> 34:57.011
-You've gone insane!
-Hey!

34:58.638 --> 35:00.765
All I've done
is exactly what you suggested.

35:00.848 --> 35:02.892
It was made with my account,
so I can do as I like.

35:03.893 --> 35:05.895
Just like your damn wishes.
You're the one who said

35:05.978 --> 35:08.022
we should separate what's mine
and what's yours!

35:08.106 --> 35:11.234
Wow. You really have totally lost it!

35:11.317 --> 35:13.694
Hey! You need to cut the crap!

35:13.778 --> 35:15.696
I'm the reason the channel
is doing well at all!

35:15.780 --> 35:16.697
Quiet.

35:17.448 --> 35:19.617
You bring the genie to me.

35:20.159 --> 35:23.204
You know it'll be erased for good
if we don't restore it within two weeks.

35:23.287 --> 35:24.247
So think carefully.

35:24.330 --> 35:26.541
I changed the password.
I'm the only one with access.

35:27.875 --> 35:30.878
Seriously, what you have just done…

35:31.587 --> 35:33.714
I hope for you that you can bring it back.

35:35.716 --> 35:37.677
This is my second wish.

35:38.261 --> 35:42.306
I want it so that Da-jin forgets
everything I said about the wishes.

35:42.390 --> 35:43.391
I wish…

35:44.517 --> 35:45.643
that she forgets everything.

35:47.395 --> 35:48.938
Right now! Are you listening?

35:49.021 --> 35:51.274
Hey. Chill out, it's been fulfilled.

35:51.357 --> 35:54.527
I was halfway across the Gobi Desert,
but sure, let me drop everything for you.

35:54.610 --> 35:57.989
You're reading this, but I know you can
hear it too. A strong, resonant voice?

35:58.072 --> 36:00.533
While we're at it, you gonna make
your final wish? What is it?

36:00.616 --> 36:03.703
Even if you've thought about it, think
harder. Be thankful I show you grace.

36:03.786 --> 36:06.414
And don't ever use words like "right now"
with me, got it?

36:22.638 --> 36:24.223
Why is the lamp not on you like I said?

36:24.807 --> 36:26.976
It's at the hotel, it's safe.
I bolted out in a rush.

36:28.394 --> 36:31.022
I came hoping I'd remember something,
but no luck.

36:32.148 --> 36:33.065
Goodness.

36:36.861 --> 36:37.862
Glad you're okay.

36:41.157 --> 36:44.035
Hug me tighter.
It could trigger something in my memory.

36:45.077 --> 36:46.245
What do you want to recall?

36:46.329 --> 36:49.582
The Muttalib from the sign over there.
Or that damn villain, Khalid.

36:50.333 --> 36:53.920
Or the joy or sorrow
we both felt in our shared past.

36:55.671 --> 36:57.798
Sensing an ulterior motive here.

36:58.591 --> 37:00.009
Says who? Squeeze tighter!

37:30.122 --> 37:30.957
You.

37:31.832 --> 37:34.502
Your clothing is unusual today.

37:35.294 --> 37:36.837
Your hair is shorter too.

37:38.714 --> 37:41.550
-Are you almost ready to leave?
-Ready to leave?

37:49.058 --> 37:50.476
You're here. Why would I leave?

37:52.770 --> 37:54.105
Do I not still owe you wishes?

37:56.065 --> 37:57.525
You certainly seem odd today.

37:58.150 --> 37:59.527
Muttalib has one wish left.

38:00.444 --> 38:03.322
You must be ready to make it.
After this, no one could be your master.

38:05.616 --> 38:08.077
That means it's time, isn't it?

38:08.577 --> 38:09.704
We can leave tonight?

38:11.372 --> 38:12.206
For Goryeo?

38:12.790 --> 38:14.542
Muttalib has a wish left?

38:33.561 --> 38:34.645
What's wrong?

38:40.318 --> 38:41.152
Hey.

38:42.737 --> 38:43.738
Where'd you go?

38:48.784 --> 38:49.994
There is a chance that…

38:52.121 --> 38:54.081
…you and I never made it to Goryeo.

38:57.376 --> 38:59.503
And I think the reason as to why

39:00.796 --> 39:02.882
is also why the sword was stuck in there.

39:05.009 --> 39:06.010
What are you saying?

39:09.513 --> 39:10.348
Oh.

39:11.599 --> 39:14.393
Why did it work for you?
Why can't I remember anything?

39:15.478 --> 39:18.356
That's not fair. Hey, swap places with me.

39:24.070 --> 39:24.904
Mm.

39:34.622 --> 39:38.250
I still feel young inside.
When did my outside become so old?

39:46.342 --> 39:48.844
Oh, my. Oh, hey!

39:48.928 --> 39:51.430
When did you get back home?
Why didn't you tell us?

39:54.016 --> 39:55.017
Hello.

39:57.228 --> 40:00.606
Oh, my. I was positive it was Pan-geum.

40:00.689 --> 40:01.982
I guess I was mistaken.

40:02.900 --> 40:05.319
Forget what I said.

40:08.030 --> 40:10.408
Why is she bothering
with a field that isn't hers?

40:19.458 --> 40:20.668
Hang on a minute.

40:27.967 --> 40:30.177
OH PAN-GEUM

40:30.261 --> 40:33.013
The person
you're trying to reach is not available.

40:33.097 --> 40:35.182
Please leave your message after the beep.

40:37.601 --> 40:39.645
Something is very strange about this.

40:40.229 --> 40:43.774
Mm. I can't imagine why
Min-ji is the only she talks to.

40:44.400 --> 40:46.652
Her husband's death anniversary
was yesterday.

40:47.319 --> 40:48.779
And she didn't even call us.

40:50.281 --> 40:51.740
No ancestral rites?

40:57.705 --> 40:58.539
Whoa…

41:00.082 --> 41:03.794
Those groceries were for the rites!
What is she doing? Huh?

41:04.795 --> 41:05.838
Oh, boy!

41:08.299 --> 41:11.844
I thought for sure you'd ask to go
to the top floor of an observation deck.

41:12.595 --> 41:14.597
I don't wanna stand
on the edge of anything.

41:16.640 --> 41:18.309
So why did your rage come out as gold?

41:18.392 --> 41:21.020
It was a truly dazzling,
beautiful hell on earth.

41:22.021 --> 41:23.731
"The wrath of Iblis" they called it.

41:23.814 --> 41:26.901
How would you say wrath manifests
for you? As gold?

41:26.984 --> 41:28.986
Gold? What do you mean?

41:29.069 --> 41:31.155
You don't remember, I don't answer. Pass.

41:36.118 --> 41:38.704
We might not remember
that time period, you or I,

41:39.455 --> 41:42.500
but we knew each other,
we spent time by each other's side.

41:42.583 --> 41:45.544
Still, Muttalib means "foreigner."

41:45.628 --> 41:49.632
We only spent time?
I thought I was your habibti, wasn't I?

41:49.715 --> 41:52.426
Our dynamic was definitely
incredibly serious.

41:52.510 --> 41:54.887
You said the odds of it being Jinniya
were 50/50.

41:57.348 --> 41:58.182
Don't tell me…

42:05.231 --> 42:07.566
-Got an umbrella?
-An umbrella?

42:11.529 --> 42:14.198
Wow, your ex is certainly meticulous.

42:15.574 --> 42:18.202
-It's raining. Kiss.
-Hey, we're in Arabia.

42:19.161 --> 42:19.995
What?

42:26.502 --> 42:28.379
You can't whisk us
somewhere it's not raining.

42:28.462 --> 42:31.382
-We haven't followed that rule for ages.
-You didn't fall for it.

42:32.299 --> 42:34.343
I'm starving.
What even is there to eat around here?

42:35.761 --> 42:39.473
-I'm so hungry, I'm about to wish for it.
-Make it.

42:39.557 --> 42:42.268
Give me a reason. Feed me now!

42:42.351 --> 42:45.145
You've never cared when I've been hungry.

42:46.438 --> 42:48.107
Change your clothes
while I set the table.

42:54.989 --> 42:56.282
Huh. Hmm.

43:02.830 --> 43:03.664
Mm!

43:17.928 --> 43:19.680
This-- This was here?

43:19.763 --> 43:23.392
Oh, no, get rid of this right now!
Burn it! No, just hide it. Let it rot.

43:23.976 --> 43:25.436
Ah, this is… Uh, maybe…

43:25.519 --> 43:27.313
Do I look like my past self?

43:29.189 --> 43:30.024
Huh?

43:48.375 --> 43:49.209
Yeah.

43:50.836 --> 43:51.712
Your past self.

43:52.755 --> 43:53.672
I do?

43:54.965 --> 43:57.760
Seems to me I also resemble
how I looked in the hourglass.

44:00.179 --> 44:01.930
Who looks nicer, current me or past me?

44:02.681 --> 44:03.891
-Uh--
-No, don't tell me.

44:03.974 --> 44:06.226
-Mm-hmm.
-Go ahead, tell me.

44:06.977 --> 44:08.604
-Uh--
-No, let's just say I am.

44:11.398 --> 44:12.232
What's that there?

44:12.858 --> 44:14.193
Huh?

44:18.864 --> 44:19.865
What?

44:27.247 --> 44:29.208
Move. It's ramyeon.

44:33.128 --> 44:35.839
Oh! I told them to prepare Korean food.

44:44.098 --> 44:46.475
-We need that fruit over here too.
-Huh? Sure.

44:52.398 --> 44:53.232
Mm.

44:55.943 --> 44:56.777
Mm.

44:58.195 --> 45:01.073
So, do you really dance the waltz
on your own? No partner?

45:02.074 --> 45:04.118
The waltz?

45:05.202 --> 45:06.328
I've never danced the waltz.

45:07.621 --> 45:08.664
I don't know how.

45:10.040 --> 45:13.419
Then how come the sandstorms in the desert
are called "the waltzing genie"?

45:14.169 --> 45:15.295
Uh…

45:17.840 --> 45:18.674
Pass.

45:24.847 --> 45:25.973
-Fine, then.
-Hmm?

45:26.557 --> 45:28.517
I'll teach you how to waltz
with a partner.

45:35.441 --> 45:38.485
Let's go. Shall we break the beat down…

45:38.569 --> 45:39.862
for old time's sake?

45:41.530 --> 45:42.573
Right.

45:53.292 --> 45:54.293
Mm?

45:55.836 --> 45:56.754
Mm?

46:06.054 --> 46:08.682
Just picture a large, round ball
squished between you and I.

46:08.766 --> 46:10.392
That ball represents a universe.

46:10.976 --> 46:13.645
The waltz is about preserving
that space. Got it?

46:14.229 --> 46:16.940
We dance around an even larger universe.

46:17.983 --> 46:20.152
-Understand?
-Yeah. I do.

46:20.235 --> 46:23.322
Look right into my eyes,
let yourself be entranced.

46:25.532 --> 46:26.658
Now, left foot goes first.

46:27.701 --> 46:31.288
-One, two, three, back.
-Okay.

46:31.371 --> 46:34.041
-One, two, three, and forward.
-Two, three…

46:34.124 --> 46:36.335
One, two--

46:37.836 --> 46:40.214
Are you gonna step on my feet like that?

46:40.798 --> 46:42.216
That's a battle, not a dance.

46:42.800 --> 46:45.135
I suppose just everything
turns into a fight with you.

46:48.096 --> 46:49.973
So, when were you first entranced by me?

46:50.057 --> 46:53.393
And one, two, three.

46:53.977 --> 46:55.395
The second time I saw you.

46:56.355 --> 46:59.483
The second time
was in the hotel room. Really?

47:00.984 --> 47:01.944
That fast?

47:03.237 --> 47:05.739
Yeah. The minute I walked in and saw you.

47:08.075 --> 47:09.284
You come after the cars I fix.

47:10.494 --> 47:14.248
-The combustion engines. Brake fluid.
-Stop, come on. Oh.

47:16.708 --> 47:18.168
The tires I rotate.

47:19.461 --> 47:21.255
-The hammer I use.
-I said, let's stop.

47:24.883 --> 47:26.009
My crowbar.

47:27.135 --> 47:29.179
Sound of dental drilling.

47:29.763 --> 47:33.433
My auto repair shop. Gamja-tang. Grandma.

48:31.700 --> 48:32.910
Pan-geum did make this.

48:34.244 --> 48:35.329
That bitch.

48:35.871 --> 48:36.955
She's here.

48:37.706 --> 48:41.126
Ouch. Why is my tooth hurting
like this?

48:41.209 --> 48:43.879
Oh, my.

48:50.010 --> 48:51.261
Why are you in my house?

48:51.929 --> 48:55.849
You better start coming clean.
Pan-geum, where is she?

48:55.933 --> 48:57.768
She-- She's in Hawaii.

48:58.352 --> 49:01.980
Don't give me that bullshit!
She's been cooking, I'm sure.

49:02.064 --> 49:04.232
Pan-geum is here, isn't she? Huh?

49:04.316 --> 49:06.443
Where are you hiding her, you con artist?

49:07.152 --> 49:08.820
Release her. I said, let her go!

49:08.904 --> 49:11.365
-I'm on to you!
-No! Why are you doing this?

49:11.448 --> 49:12.824
-Let go of me!
-Hey!

49:12.908 --> 49:15.285
Where do you think you're going?
Get back here!

49:16.411 --> 49:18.872
Oh, that mole!

49:18.956 --> 49:20.832
Pan-geum has a mole on her body too!

49:21.333 --> 49:23.335
What have you done? Huh?

49:23.418 --> 49:25.462
Are you Pan-geum?

49:26.213 --> 49:28.757
-You're Pan-geum?
-No, you're wrong!

49:30.676 --> 49:32.386
-Seongnim!
-Seongnim!

49:32.469 --> 49:33.553
Oh!

49:34.179 --> 49:37.057
You are Pan-geum! You are!

49:37.849 --> 49:39.685
It's Pan-geum!

49:40.268 --> 49:42.562
Seongnim! Seongnim!

49:42.646 --> 49:44.147
Oh, my goodness!

49:44.231 --> 49:46.817
-How'd this even happen?
-Seongnim! Seongnim!

49:47.985 --> 49:50.112
Seongnim. Listen to me.
I beg of you. You have to--

49:50.195 --> 49:52.072
Let go, you absolute devil!

49:52.155 --> 49:54.074
Let go of me! Lord!

49:55.283 --> 49:56.868
You were Pan-geum all along.

49:56.952 --> 49:58.870
I spent so much time worrying.

49:58.954 --> 50:00.956
What did you do? How the hell…

50:01.039 --> 50:04.501
-How the hell did you pull this off? Huh?
-I'll confess everything.

50:04.584 --> 50:07.879
I swear! I beg you!
I beg you, please don't tell anybody!

50:07.963 --> 50:09.423
-Please!
-You disgust me!

50:09.506 --> 50:12.342
Let go, you witch! What's happening?

50:13.051 --> 50:15.595
Oh, God, Seongnim. Oh, no!

50:24.187 --> 50:26.565
What? That bitch is Oh Pan-geum?

50:27.149 --> 50:30.485
That's how she managed to keep her hidden.

50:31.570 --> 50:34.573
Ah! That's how Ka-young used her wish.

50:34.656 --> 50:37.200
Let's get rid of
the old lady anyway, please?

50:37.284 --> 50:40.203
She'll just run her mouth
otherwise. Ishrun.

50:40.829 --> 50:42.664
Remember the way to the house?

50:47.753 --> 50:49.880
One, two, three.

50:50.589 --> 50:52.382
Two, two, three.

50:53.842 --> 50:55.010
It's time to go home.

50:56.178 --> 50:59.264
I'll go and get changed.
They've dried, right?

51:00.640 --> 51:01.516
Of course.

51:06.897 --> 51:11.318
One, two, three. Two, two, three.

51:11.401 --> 51:12.319
One, two--
